      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We apply the competitive model of Loxley and Robinson (Phys Rev Lett 102:258701, 2009. doi: 10.1103/PhysRevLett.102.258701 ) to the study of a special case of visual rivalry. Three-peaked inputs with maxima at symmetrical locations are introduced, and the role of three-bump configurations is then considered. The model yields conditions for what can be interpreted as a bistable percept analogous to the one-dimensional version of a competition between the central and flanking parts of an image."},
